#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95de501c-c29d-5cbf-9a79-048a79089948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95de501c-c29d-5cbf-9a79-048a79089948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517771} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7ff32db-e290-547d-9167-5bfd000c5b9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b40960a4-3462-5880-9ff6-2c1313bf33f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-171905" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bd6b42e1d48ca0e45ffc9b8910345bea52f1f44f9754f00ac4a4ba034e273bb5.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3x+(2x+{20}^{∘})+(5x-{24}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 14x-{4}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 14x & ={364}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={26}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0794b384-c2ff-5d4a-b325-28077b5b1f96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Quantity Using Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e08b8587-2673-5d67-85be-e9c69a264b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e08b8587-2673-5d67-85be-e9c69a264b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517910} :answer-field/id #uuid "525a4469-4e3e-58b4-bc94-04e70a60046c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e54967a4-313f-5425-b80c-928ee57bb212" :question/math-academy-id "q-223198" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a92c3df4f9d410b1a7620cf43b04fda1ce7312cebd8c6077a0b0411ecc78ad73.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2x+(x+{10}^{∘})+(2x-{10}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a27d61-a734-57ce-a1b9-e6a9d52463e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{155}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517553} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccb46db-67ff-50b8-8b68-b38569111f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{168}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517791} {:answer/id #uuid "aefd51f3-7fe9-58df-9f1a-21094a7ee66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{152}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517818} {:answer/id #uuid "df4121c9-1388-5799-80fd-0cbb19b668e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{173}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517909} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7972ee-be19-5bae-a8dd-d693c56fe478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{163}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22a27d61-a734-57ce-a1b9-e6a9d52463e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{155}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517553} :answer-field/id #uuid "b89379c4-d191-53ca-8ac5-ec0071d31fd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "143c348d-4bc6-5a45-bf95-01d78dce959f" :question/math-academy-id "q-223201" :question/problem "![](images/33/33c1016cb2353e5332a5e04e8f377d4fa7d76e1b569a3532a45c5a068cc6d255.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6x+{23}^{∘})+(17x-{4}^{∘})+(21x+{8}^{∘})+(4x-{3}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 48x+{24}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 48x & ={336}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={7}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x+{8}^{∘} & =21({7}^{∘})+{8}^{∘} \\\\  & ={147}^{∘}+8 \\\\  & ={155}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64712488-234f-5d44-92a9-6a4821f2d304" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Exterior Angle by Determining an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b680264-dfb5-59a3-bcc8-c4eaa88b0281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b680264-dfb5-59a3-bcc8-c4eaa88b0281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517512} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7c212c7-8e24-558b-a30f-86787ad1fb45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da26be71-f6d6-5898-b94d-3e43f1a50c61" :question/math-academy-id "q-223237" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c8bc8341b9619e9fddb151b02d2d859fab801fe35114de6b2ce6d09045fff11.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $B$ is ${180}^{∘}-(4x+{18}^{∘})={162}^{∘}-4x.$\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x+{15}^{∘})+({162}^{∘}-4x)+(4x-{2}^{∘})+(3x+{1}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{176}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={184}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={23}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{2}^{∘} & =4({23}^{∘})-{2}^{∘} \\\\  & ={92}^{∘}-{2}^{∘} \\\\  & ={90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5de9bf2f-b11c-5af0-a569-5f25aebae227" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Exterior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6318460b-5678-5646-a910-82e6cf183480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6318460b-5678-5646-a910-82e6cf183480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517670} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cb61399-54db-53c5-9e53-bf360481e48d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ac19296-c890-536b-9e9a-47b0cd74c840" :question/math-academy-id "q-223356" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e40dfd3842ec7a7b5de16d7938988e86209960ae9cba510bbac004b0bb73d94.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠B$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $∠B.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{58}^{∘}+x+{65}^{∘}+{63}^{∘}+{97}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x+{283}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={77}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
